course: dictionary
lesson: 3466
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Fairy is one of them. To choose the right meaning, read the words around it and ask which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: In a story, a fairy is a tiny magic person with wings. «In Hansel and Gretel, an old fairy tale collected by the Brothers Grimm, Hansel drops breadcrumbs to find the way home.» The words fairy tale and the story tell you that fairy means magic here.
explain: Fairy can also describe another word, as in «fairy lights» and «fairy cake». Here fairy tells you what kind of light or cake it is, so it is an adjective. Fairy lights are small electric lights, not magic people.
explain: When you meet a word with two meanings, try each meaning in the sentence. The one that makes the most sense is the right one.
fact: Fairy can be a noun (fairy, fairies) or an adjective (fairy).
fact: A fairy is a tiny magic person with wings in stories.
fact: Fairy lights are small electric lights on a string, used for decoration.
fact: A fairy tale is a magic story for children.
fact: In maths, «each fairy has 2 wings» is a rate, so you multiply: 3 fairies have 6 wings.
exercise: «Each fairy has 2 wings.» How many wings do 4 fairies have? | 2 | 6 | *8 | 4
exercise: In «an old fairy tale collected by the Brothers Grimm», what kind of story is a fairy tale? | *A magic story for children | A recipe for cake | A true news report | A maths lesson
exercise: Mum hangs fairy lights on the tree. What are fairy lights? | *Small electric lights on a string for decoration | Wings | A cake for parties | A kind of tiny magic person
test: In «fairy cake», what kind of word is fairy? | Adverb | Noun | *Adjective | Verb
test: «In Britain and the USA the tooth fairy swaps a lost tooth for a coin.» Which meaning of fairy is this? | *A magic character in a story | Something made of wings | Fairy lights | A fairy cake
exam: In the phrase «fairy godmother», what does fairy mean? | A type of tree | *Magic, from stories | A small electric light | A cake shaped like a tooth
